  "sign_convention": "Positive cup change is a gain. Positive image shift is downward, which indicates withdrawal. Each comparison joins consecutive saved endpoints.",
  "primary_method": [
    "Register each pair to both columns of stationary red graduations. At each image row interpolate the vertical shift of neighboring matching ticks at each column, then interpolate laterally. A whole-cup affine fit supplies horizontal registration.",
    "A manually identified near-wall contact arc defines each search band. Each nonoverlapping window spans 59 native pixels. Pick falling red/green intensity profiles in the before frame, mask printed ink in both frames and match the same profiles vertically with a local brightness offset. For larger shifts, independently marked curves locate the search band in each frame. Use the median across readable windows.",
    "Convert each downward shift with the local difference between the neighboring printed volumes divided by their native vertical spacing. Blend the two local column sensitivities between columns and use the nearest column sensitivity outside. The low-fill right column uses the nearest visible interval below its lowest printed mark."
  ],
  "alternatives": [
    "Repeat with an affine fit to all corresponding marks and measure with the intensity-gradient centroid across the same local edge. Compare full-view and independent half-view medians for all four combinations.",
    "Where available, fit the near-wall arc independently in each full image and calculate the difference using six positions on the two front scales. This second estimator uses the cup volume marks directly and is sensitive to which portions of the contact remain visible."
  ],
